WEBVTT

1
00:00:30.416 --> 00:00:31.958
<b>In all previous verses,</b>

2
00:00:31.958 --> 00:00:36.083
<b>Lord Krishna has consistently guided</b>
<b>Arjuna towards performing</b>

3
00:00:36.083 --> 00:00:39.333
<b>selfless action (Nishkam Karma) </b>
<b>without attachment to results.</b>

4
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:40.166
<b>Now, here</b>

5
00:00:40.166 --> 00:00:43.958
<b>for the first time, Krishna is inspiring Arjuna </b>
<b>to rise above even selfless action</b>

6
00:00:43.958 --> 00:00:47.875
<b>to reach the level of devotional service.</b>

7
00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:56.125
<b>Lord Krishna has, until now,</b>

8
00:00:56.125 --> 00:01:01.125
<b>to fight this war, without any attachment, </b>
<b>seeing it merely as his duty</b>

9
00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:03.875
<b>Now, Krishna tells Arjuna</b>

10
00:01:03.875 --> 00:01:09.708
<b>to dedicate all his selfless actions </b>
<b>to Him with complete devotion.</b>

11
00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:13.291
<b>This verse mentions three essential qualities:</b>

12
00:01:13.291 --> 00:01:15.375
<b>First - Nirashi</b>

13
00:01:15.375 --> 00:01:20.750
<b>- Acting without expectation of </b>
<b>material desires or gains</b>

14
00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:22.666
<b>Second - Nirmam</b>

15
00:01:22.666 --> 00:01:26.833
<b>- Free from ownership and ego</b>

16
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:27.750
<b>and</b>

17
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.708
<b>Third - Vigat Jwar</b>

18
00:01:29.708 --> 00:01:34.125
<b>- Free from lethargy and agitation</b>

19
00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:38.125
<b>Krishna desires that whatever </b>
<b>actions Arjuna performs,</b>

20
00:01:38.125 --> 00:01:39.500
<b>whatever battle he fights,</b>

21
00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.208
<b>should be done with these three qualities –</b>

22
00:01:43.208 --> 00:01:50.416
<b>free from expectations, free from ego, </b>
<b>and free from both lethargy and agitation.</b>

23
00:01:50.416 --> 00:01:52.541
<b>This becomes possible</b>

24
00:01:52.541 --> 00:01:57.000
<b>only when Arjuna's consciousness </b>
<b>is centered on Lord Krishna.</b>

25
00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:00.583
<b>He will begin to realize </b>
<b>that everything he has today –</b>

26
00:02:00.583 --> 00:02:01.583
<b>this body,</b>

27
00:02:01.583 --> 00:02:03.583
<b>this world, everything</b>

28
00:02:03.583 --> 00:02:05.333
<b>- is given by the Lord.</b>

29
00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:08.083
<b>And if everything is given by Lord Krishna,</b>

30
00:02:08.083 --> 00:02:15.291
<b>then isn't it appropriate to offer the </b>
<b>fruits of selfless action at His feet?</b>

31
00:02:15.291 --> 00:02:19.833
<b>Through this practice, one rises above the </b>
<b>level of selfless action (Nishkam Karma Yoga) </b>

32
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:23.333
<b>and progresses toward the path of </b>
<b>devotional service (Bhakti Yoga).</b>

33
00:02:23.333 --> 00:02:25.875
<b>Performing actions without attachment to results,</b>

34
00:02:25.875 --> 00:02:29.916
<b>and offering whatever fruits arise to the Lord –</b>

35
00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:32.083
<b>how liberating is this thought!</b>

36
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:36.625
<b>A solution that frees us from worldly bondage.</b>

37
00:02:36.625 --> 00:02:38.541
<b>To perform actions with devotion</b>

38
00:02:38.541 --> 00:02:41.375
<b>and offer them at Krishna's feet –</b>

39
00:02:41.375 --> 00:02:45.541
<b>this is indeed the highest level of selfless action."</b>

40
00:02:50.041 --> 00:02:51.791
<b>In life,</b>

41
00:02:51.791 --> 00:02:57.791
<b>you perform various actions </b>
<b>- some small, some large.</b>

42
00:02:57.791 --> 00:03:00.833
<b>Helping someone at home,</b>

43
00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:03.166
<b>assisting a neighbor,</b>

44
00:03:03.166 --> 00:03:04.166
<b>or</b>

45
00:03:04.166 --> 00:03:14.666
<b>listening and guiding a friend </b>
<b>who's troubled or confused.</b>

46
00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:16.000
<b>Fundamentally,</b>

47
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:19.416
<b>humans possess many good qualities.</b>

48
00:03:19.416 --> 00:03:22.625
<b>The only dilemma is that</b>

49
00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:29.416
<b>often, they perform these acts </b>
<b>expecting something in return.</b>

50
00:03:29.416 --> 00:03:31.875
<b>"Family members will praise me,"</b>

51
00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:34.833
<b>"If I help my neighbor today,</b>

52
00:03:34.833 --> 00:03:37.666
<b>they'll help me tomorrow,"</b>

53
00:03:37.666 --> 00:03:45.708
<b>"If I assist a friend now, </b>
<b>they'll return the favor later."</b>

54
00:03:45.708 --> 00:03:47.250
<b>Though small,</b>

55
00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:52.541
<b>self-interest lurks even here.</b>

56
00:03:52.541 --> 00:03:54.666
<b>Now consider this:</b>

57
00:03:54.666 --> 00:04:00.666
<b>what if you help someone at home</b>

58
00:04:00.666 --> 00:04:02.875
<b>simply because you are capable</b>

59
00:04:02.875 --> 00:04:09.625
<b>and genuinely wish to contribute </b>
<b>to another's well-being?</b>

60
00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:13.625
<b>This perspective will transform </b>
<b>your entire outlook.</b>

61
00:04:13.625 --> 00:04:21.083
<b>You'll find immense satisfaction </b>
<b>and joy in helping others.</b>

62
00:04:21.083 --> 00:04:22.666
<b>Because now, </b>

63
00:04:22.666 --> 00:04:26.291
<b>you're free from bondage.</b>

64
00:04:26.291 --> 00:04:30.416
<b>If you help someone</b>

65
00:04:30.416 --> 00:04:33.625
<b>expecting their help in return,</b>

66
00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:39.666
<b>aren't you bound by that expectation?</b>

67
00:04:39.666 --> 00:04:43.750
<b>And if tomorrow you don't receive help in return,</b>

68
00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.333
<b>bitterness will creep in,</b>

69
00:04:46.333 --> 00:04:52.166
<b>making you hesitate to help others in the future.</b>

70
00:04:52.166 --> 00:04:55.375
<b>In this scenario, whose </b>
<b>thinking becomes polluted,</b>

71
00:04:55.375 --> 00:04:58.375
<b>who becomes frustrated?</b>

72
00:04:58.375 --> 00:05:01.333
<b>It’s only you right?</b>

73
00:05:01.333 --> 00:05:02.875
<b>But if</b>

74
00:05:02.875 --> 00:05:07.041
<b>you helped without expecting anything in return,</b>

75
00:05:07.041 --> 00:05:13.291
<b>such frustration and thoughts </b>
<b>wouldn't even come near you.</b>

76
00:05:13.291 --> 00:05:17.625
<b>You'll continue supporting</b>
<b>others with a pure heart,</b>

77
00:05:17.625 --> 00:05:20.291
<b>performing your duties,</b>

78
00:05:20.291 --> 00:05:24.208
<b>free from all bondage.</b>

79
00:05:24.208 --> 00:05:27.583
<b>Start this experiment today.</b>

80
00:05:27.583 --> 00:05:30.833
<b>Begin with small acts of assistance.</b>

81
00:05:30.833 --> 00:05:35.375
<b>Without ego, help someone daily</b>

82
00:05:35.375 --> 00:05:41.333
<b>who can't give you anything in return.</b>

83
00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:43.166
<b>Then observe</b>

84
00:05:43.166 --> 00:05:47.583
<b>the joy you experience.</b>

85
00:05:47.583 --> 00:05:49.291
<b>I am with you.</b>

86
00:05:49.291 --> 00:05:52.166
<b>Take this first step.</b>

87
00:05:56.625 --> 00:06:00.750
<b>In relationships with family and friends,</b>

88
00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:07.000
<b>we often develop a tendency to control.</b>

89
00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:11.333
<b>Sometimes we might feel</b>

90
00:06:11.333 --> 00:06:20.875
<b>that family members and friends </b>
<b>should behave exactly as we prefer.</b>

91
00:06:20.875 --> 00:06:22.833
<b>For example –</b>

92
00:06:22.833 --> 00:06:26.583
<b>when planning a trip somewhere,</b>

93
00:06:26.583 --> 00:06:30.333
<b>we become disturbed by the mere fact</b>

94
00:06:30.333 --> 00:06:35.875
<b>that not everyone wants to</b>
<b>visit our suggested destination.</b>

95
00:06:35.875 --> 00:06:39.000
<b>We try to ensure our opinion is heard,</b>

96
00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.833
<b>that the location is chosen</b>
<b>according to our preference,</b>

97
00:06:41.833 --> 00:06:45.625
<b>and that everyone agrees with it.</b>

98
00:06:45.625 --> 00:06:48.500
<b>But consider this:</b>

99
00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:54.625
<b>what if we abandon this sense of </b>
<b>control in these relationships?</b>

100
00:06:54.625 --> 00:06:56.541
<b>How would that be?</b>

101
00:06:56.541 --> 00:07:02.000
<b>This doesn't mean we should become silent,</b>

102
00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.666
<b>step back,</b>

103
00:07:03.666 --> 00:07:10.083
<b>and merely agree with whatever group </b>
<b>decision emerges without truly feeling it.</b>

104
00:07:10.083 --> 00:07:16.791
<b>Abandoning control doesn't </b>
<b>mean abandoning your duty.</b>

105
00:07:16.791 --> 00:07:22.416
<b>In this example, your duty is </b>
<b>to present your perspective,</b>

106
00:07:22.416 --> 00:07:28.583
<b>to explain what you find appealing </b>
<b>about your suggested destination.</b>

107
00:07:28.583 --> 00:07:30.416
<b>However,</b>

108
00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:33.166
<b>being rigid about your suggestion,</b>

109
00:07:33.166 --> 00:07:39.958
<b>trying to control the group - that's attachment.</b>

110
00:07:39.958 --> 00:07:43.208
<b>You are a participant in such situations,</b>

111
00:07:43.208 --> 00:07:47.208
<b>not an owner or controller.</b>

112
00:07:47.208 --> 00:07:50.125
<b>This was just a small example,</b>

113
00:07:50.125 --> 00:07:51.708
<b>but this thinking</b>

114
00:07:51.708 --> 00:07:56.166
<b>can be extremely helpful in family settings.</b>

115
00:07:56.166 --> 00:07:59.666
<b>Take parenting, for instance.</b>

116
00:07:59.666 --> 00:08:04.833
<b>Often, parents try to control</b>

117
00:08:04.833 --> 00:08:07.916
<b>what their children will do in life,</b>

118
00:08:07.916 --> 00:08:10.041
<b>what subjects they'll study,</b>

119
00:08:10.041 --> 00:08:14.041
<b>what interests they should develop.</b>

120
00:08:14.041 --> 00:08:19.625
<b>This too is a form of control and ownership.</b>

121
00:08:19.625 --> 00:08:25.416
<b>Here, if parents choose the path </b>
<b>of participation instead of control,</b>

122
00:08:25.416 --> 00:08:27.750
<b>share their experiences,</b>

123
00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:31.416
<b>and allow children to make decisions,</b>

124
00:08:31.416 --> 00:08:35.458
<b>it will not only boost the children's self-confidence</b>

125
00:08:35.458 --> 00:08:36.291
<b>but</b>

126
00:08:36.291 --> 00:08:40.375
<b>also increase their respect </b>
<b>and love for their parents.</b>

127
00:08:40.375 --> 00:08:44.791
<b>Control in relationships </b>
<b>always becomes an obstacle.</b>

128
00:08:44.791 --> 00:08:46.041
<b>Whereas</b>

129
00:08:46.041 --> 00:08:48.458
<b>participation and dialogue –</b>

130
00:08:48.458 --> 00:08:52.458
<b>these two strengthen relationships.</b>

131
00:08:52.458 --> 00:08:54.375
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

132
00:08:58.833 --> 00:09:01.375
<b>In modern organizations</b>

133
00:09:01.375 --> 00:09:04.041
<b>and today's workplaces,</b>

134
00:09:04.041 --> 00:09:08.250
<b>there's an extremely competitive atmosphere.</b>

135
00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:10.041
<b>Everyone is racing,</b>

136
00:09:10.041 --> 00:09:15.208
<b>which ultimately leads to stress and exhaustion.</b>

137
00:09:15.208 --> 00:09:18.708
<b>This verse indicates that</b>

138
00:09:18.708 --> 00:09:23.416
<b>we should perform our work </b>
<b>with complete dedication</b>

139
00:09:23.416 --> 00:09:26.625
<b>and in a spirit of devotion.</b>

140
00:09:26.625 --> 00:09:33.541
<b> Will progress at work come from being </b>
<b>constantly consumed by competitive worry?</b>

141
00:09:33.541 --> 00:09:34.958
<b>No.</b>

142
00:09:34.958 --> 00:09:39.958
<b>Progress will come when your work quality is high,</b>

143
00:09:39.958 --> 00:09:47.041
<b>when your work plays an important role </b>
<b>in achieving organizational goals.</b>

144
00:09:47.041 --> 00:09:48.416
<b>Dedication</b>

145
00:09:48.416 --> 00:09:51.416
<b>and devotion.</b>

146
00:09:51.416 --> 00:09:57.916
<b>Dedication to your work will elevate its quality,</b>

147
00:09:57.916 --> 00:10:03.458
<b>While work done with devotion </b>
<b>is being offered to the Divine.</b>

148
00:10:03.458 --> 00:10:07.416
<b>You're also offering it to the organization.</b>

149
00:10:07.416 --> 00:10:11.250
<b>In this way, your purpose rises</b>
<b>from personal progress</b>

150
00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:14.458
<b>to collective organizational growth.</b>

151
00:10:14.458 --> 00:10:16.708
<b>Think of it this way –</b>

152
00:10:16.708 --> 00:10:22.333
<b>even your smallest task is</b>
<b>for someone else's welfare.</b>

153
00:10:22.333 --> 00:10:24.041
<b>For example,</b>

154
00:10:24.041 --> 00:10:30.083
<b>if a very senior officer simply </b>
<b>spends some time with colleagues,</b>

155
00:10:30.083 --> 00:10:32.583
<b>asking about their well-being,</b>

156
00:10:32.583 --> 00:10:36.250
<b>many might consider this a trivial matter.</b>

157
00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:39.458
<b>But think again...</b>

158
00:10:39.458 --> 00:10:44.125
<b>if such behavior encourages a colleague,</b>

159
00:10:44.125 --> 00:10:46.625
<b>gives them a positive experience,</b>

160
00:10:46.625 --> 00:10:50.333
<b>isn't that beneficial for them?</b>

161
00:10:50.333 --> 00:10:51.958
<b>And ultimately,</b>

162
00:10:51.958 --> 00:10:57.875
<b>such a positive environment </b>
<b>will impact work quality too.</b>

163
00:10:57.875 --> 00:11:01.166
<b> And if work quality improves,</b>

164
00:11:01.166 --> 00:11:04.958
<b>it benefits the organization's customers.</b>

165
00:11:04.958 --> 00:11:10.291
<b>Looking deeper, customer welfare </b>
<b>is embedded in this too.</b>

166
00:11:10.291 --> 00:11:12.416
<b>Whether the work is small or large,</b>

167
00:11:12.416 --> 00:11:17.583
<b>isn't its ultimate purpose someone's welfare?</b>

168
00:11:17.583 --> 00:11:23.000
<b>This too is a form of dedication, a form of devotion.</b>

169
00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:24.750
<b>Adopting such thinking</b>

170
00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:30.500
<b>will keep your focus solely on </b>
<b>the work, on improving it,</b>

171
00:11:30.500 --> 00:11:32.916
<b>finding satisfaction in it.</b>

172
00:11:32.916 --> 00:11:33.833
<b>And</b>

173
00:11:33.833 --> 00:11:38.250
<b>you'll be free from unnecessary </b>
<b>competition and stress.</b>

174
00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:39.666
<b>Moreover,</b>

175
00:11:39.666 --> 00:11:43.583
<b>if you work with dedication to the organization,</b>

176
00:11:43.583 --> 00:11:48.791
<b>the organization will ultimately respond.</b>

177
00:11:48.791 --> 00:11:51.125
<b>Success will come naturally,</b>

178
00:11:51.125 --> 00:11:55.958
<b>whether you chase it or not.</b>

179
00:11:55.958 --> 00:11:57.208
<b>This Gita,</b>

180
00:11:57.208 --> 00:11:59.000
<b>its teachings,</b>

181
00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:03.458
<b>and this devotion will bring you peace of mind,</b>

182
00:12:03.458 --> 00:12:05.333
<b>and when the mind is peaceful,</b>

183
00:12:05.333 --> 00:12:10.708
<b>choosing the right path in </b>
<b>every situation becomes easier.</b>

184
00:12:10.708 --> 00:12:14.666
<b>Dedication and devotion.</b>

185
00:12:14.666 --> 00:12:16.500
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

